Save93 equipment comparison of two stricter accelerate rules, 2026-11-10 / AE 1.6.1170 / SSE Display Tweaks limiter 30 FPS (42 FPS for xh-42), DynamicUpdateBudget=false / Papyrus bEnableLogging=0, bEnableProfiling=1
APB_CATCHUP_MODE=accelerate, APB_CATCHUP_TARGET=60, EngageBelowFPS 50. Catch-up is ON in every trial; "off" trials are the release rule, "on" trials the test rule named by the trace mode in each run header.
  catchup-holdcalls (xh-*): a queued native that is judged a change is itself kept out of the extra cycles (VMCatchUp::SetHoldChangeCalls; needs the test-only hook on AttemptFunctionCall +0x633, Settings::observeQueuedCalls).
  catchup-allowlist (xa0-30): natives judged by the read list alone, which in that build held only the helper natives (the floor).
  catchup-allowlist (xa52-*): the same with the 52-entry measurement list (IsListedReadNative; entries chosen from the census, implementations NOT reviewed).
  catchup-strict (xs-*): both test rules together, 52-entry list.
Test DLLs: xh-*, xa0-30 APBGameplayTrace.dll sha256 b7791536e843d71530a0bcd203d0940290a8d6b4056c15da71041b388d4c6d18 (14:55 build); xa52-*, xs-* sha256 965edbafb80ad6827a622ffb4985b69300efab25a7a76f77a1cb31197951c9af (15:22 build). The release plugin calls none of the test controls.
Order off,on,on,off,on,off,off,on per launch (build/catchup/run-effect-ab.ps1). foreground_pct was 100.0 in 56 trials. The xa0-30 launch (the floor) ran with the game window NOT in front (0.0 in its eight trials), so its times are not comparable with the others; its result rests on the extra-cycle count (1-6 per trial against 132-140 in the release trials of the same launch). guard_violations and overrun_pauses were 0 in all 64.
Reference without catch-up, same day and scene (verification/Save93-VMCatchUp-Effect-1338-Build.log): 174 handlers 1259-1358 ms, 202/203 handlers 1958-2058 ms at 30 FPS.
Census of the natives this run calls: verification/Save93-Native-Census-2026-11-10.log.

